<title>BELGIUM: EU finance ministers agree to readmit lira.</title>
<headline>EU finance ministers agree to readmit lira.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS, Belgium</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance ministers and central bank governors from the European Union, meeting in emergency session, agreed Sunday to readmit the Italian lira to the EU's exchange rate mechanism.</p>
<p>European Union officials said the ministers agreed to allow the lira to return to the currency grid at a rate of 990 lira to the German mark, lower than the 1,000 lira that Rome had been seeking.</p>
</text>
